From 3b61ebf076f0a9ba969471a3bd64173fb81deef4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:16:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] Real-world evaluation fixes: export-macro heads, TEST()
 bodies, fallthrough/VLA/null-branch false alarms, float in
 interval/fuzz/replay, '#' in strings

Measured on jsmn, tinyexpr and cJSON (docs/EVALUATION.md):
- cparse (both engines): a leading export macro (JSMN_API int f) and a
  function-like one wrapping the return type (CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON *) f) no
  longer leave the whole public API as PARSE-GAP; ALL_CAPS macro bodies
  such as TEST(Suite, Name) { ... } are parsed as OTHER functions, so the
  lints see test bodies. testdata_tp/parse_gap.c now uses a lowercase
  macro head for its gap (premise change: TEST(alloc) is parsed now and
  its planted UAF is found, see realworld_twins.c).
- CTRL-FALLTHROUGH: char-literal labels (case '}'), #ifdef lines between
  stacked labels, GCC comment annotations (Falls through.), and the last
  arm of a switch are not fallthroughs (regex layer); the AST layer
  accepts 'falls through' comments too.
- MEM-VLA-SIZE: bounds of literals, sizeof and never-assigned ALL_CAPS
  names (BUFSIZ, MAX_LEN * 2 + 1) are constant.
- PTR-NULL-DEREF: the then-branch of 'if (!n) return;' is that line only,
  and a braced branch ends at its own brace (the else arm is not in it).
- interval: float/double parameters and locals are outside the integer
  domain (was INT-SIGNED-OVF on double a + b).
- fuzz (FuSeBMC concrete loop) and execute (cex replay): float/double
  functions are NEEDS-HARNESS (was CRASH INT-SIGNED-OVF on double sum1).
- concrete interpreter: only directive lines are preprocessor, not '#'
  inside a string (was concolic ERROR on test(t, "issue #22")).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
