From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:28:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] warnings: compile_commands flags, parallel units,
 missing header is NOTRUN; fuzz: no re-run of identical inputs

- warnings (C++): each unit gets the -I/-D/-std= of its compile_commands.json
  entry (else -I root and root/include, as the Clang-AST lints guess);
  (compiler, unit) checks run on --jobs threads like the Python engine's
  ordered_map; a fatal 'header not found' is NOTRUN (the include path is
  unknown), not FAILED compiler-error and not 'gcc unusable: failed to
  start' (gcc's 'No such file or directory' tripped tool_unusable).
  Python engine: the same NOTRUN row.
- fuzz (FuSeBMC concrete loop): an input already run is not run again
  (deterministic oracle; a no-parameter function has one input), and
  without --allow-exec a round with the previous round's seeds is not
  repeated. cJSON: the fuzz stage spent 772 s re-running Unity test
  functions with no parameters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PNtqaD75q6kS9GMoczxQVx
