Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:14:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] interval: integer literal suffixes and unmodelled local
 declarations (both engines)

tinyexpr: 'st * 6364136223846793005ULL' alarmed INT-SIGNED-OVF before the
split-off ULL token was seen, and 'unsigned long int un = ..., ur, i;'
left its names untracked so 'un - ur' read a signed full range. A U
suffix now makes the literal unsigned; an L/LL literal and a declaration
the engine does not parse are unencoded (ParseFail: no interval finding
for that function; pir still checks it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PNtqaD75q6kS9GMoczxQVx
