From 71a58d3e67ede8be3c077c57e839f937e083f948 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:26:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] cparse (both engines): zlib K&R definitions were
 dropped without a gap

zlib 1.2.12: deflate.c 15 of 30 bodies, trees.c 6 of 22, crc32.c 9 of 22
were neither functions nor PARSE-GAP rows (a Law 7 hole):
- a lowercase storage macro before the type ('local block_state
  deflate_stored(s, flush)', #define local static) is taken as a modifier;
- K&R parameter declarations may be function pointers ('void (*init)(void);');
- an #if/#else whose arms each open a brace ('#ifdef FORCE_STORED if (..) {
  #else if (..) { #endif') keeps only its first arm for brace matching
  (bodies keep every arm); balanced conditionals are untouched;
- a top-level '{' whose head is K&R text the patterns cannot read is now a
  PARSE-GAP at the head's line instead of a silently skipped body.
Both engines produce identical inventory/classify rows on zlib, cJSON,
jsmn, tinyexpr, cxxopts and testdata/ (unchanged there).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PNtqaD75q6kS9GMoczxQVx
