From 1cad5e4ee44f2c1a229f0df01d6312e9879cb970 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:09:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] pir: compile_commands include paths, missing header
 NOTRUN; bounded query normalisation; concolic C++ names; STR-NULL-ARG guards

- pir (C++): each unit is lowered with the -I/-D/... of its
  compile_commands.json entry (never its -std=), else with the scan root
  and root/include after the system headers (-idirafter). A missing header
  is NOTRUN 'does not compile standalone', not ERROR 'clang front end
  failed' (cxxopts: every unit under src/ and test/ was ERROR).
- solver query normalisation (the cache key) ran Z3's simplifier with no
  time bound: on zlib crc32.c one call ran over 15 minutes, past every
  --timeout, and zlib did not finish in an hour. It now has 10 s; past it
  the unsimplified formula keys the cache.
- concolic (both engines): a C++ qualified name in the body is
  NEEDS-HARNESS (Catch2 was ERROR 'expected ) got :').
- STR-NULL-ARG and the other lints that ask whether a pointer parameter
  was NULL-tested (both engines): a test inside a larger condition counts
  ('if (object->valuestring == NULL || valuestring == NULL)', the fix of
